  "interpretation": "Current topology exposes the two late-ramp targets before leader entry, but the 120 m conditional stopping margins are insufficient in ramp-44 and fragile in ramp-50. Expanded 240 m context offers earlier supported projections; it is an additional information requirement, not demonstrated sensing or a validated control fix. A deficit marks failure of this response profile, not proof that no other response is possible.",
  "next_action": "Predeclare a bounded preview-control contract: observation range and uncertainty, conditional lateral-path handling, positive braking reserve, other-motion assumptions, recovery and native safety authority. Then test matched development interventions with full controlled/human/ramp/external burdens before any comfort acceptance; keep geometry qualification and v04 handoff separate.",
  "limits": "One previously inspected synthetic seed; provisional geometry; exact simulator positions and map; expanded 240 m range is not demonstrated sensing/communication. Conditional lateral projection has no merge-time or intent evidence. Braking models are assumptions; other road users, SUMO intervention and delayed insertions are not counterfactually resolved. No rollout, actor, training, protected audit inspection or shared writes.",
  "methodological_notes": [
    "120 m matches the prior nominal radius, not an identical observation set: this diagnostic uses Euclidean inclusion and all reachable incoming same/adjacent paths; the old front-neighbor margin used directed lane gaps and nearest candidates.",
    "Only positive projected front-position differences receive a front stopping envelope. Rear and exactly side-by-side candidates remain in journals without a front-envelope assessment; absence of a deficit is not a safe label.",
    "First supported projection is not first warning. Negative margin means the constructed profile already lacks reserve. Earliest support/deficit labels are retrospective and limited to the predeclared 10 s window.",
    "Signals use lane, lane position, length, speed, acceleration and x/y only. IDs identify records; routes, roles, schedules, observed future motion and native leader labels do not select candidates.",
    "Unknown initial braking profiles remain unknown. Primary/drain counts, all leader switches and all jerk episodes are retained. No protected observations or new simulator trajectory were read/generated."
  ],
